 "notes": "Clean-steel battle HUD over a side-on parallax battlefield (no modal frame). Top-left: teal lantern banner hangs from a rod at the top edge and overlaps the left ends of two stacked dark-steel bar plates (hull on top, courage below; both start behind the banner at x 86 and end in a pointed right tip). Each plate: round dark socket with icon (red heart / orange flame), bronze-edged track, fill, and a right-aligned white Crimson value. Hull fill is teal-green (240 / 300; the drawn fill reaches ~86% of the track interior, not exactly 80%), courage fill is blue (66 / 100, matches 66%). Top-right: gold plaque with pointed left end, coin icon, cream value and a thin vertical divider; the plaque fades out to the right behind the octagonal pause button. Card dock: bronze-edged dark frame bottom-centre with small arrow ornaments at its lower corners; five 119x131 cards on a 132 px pitch, each with full-bleed art, a round brown cost badge with gold ring at the top-right and a white Crimson number. Selected state: card.1 (shield knight, cost 20) is drawn larger (128x142, rising to the dock's top edge) with a thick glowing gold frame and a gold diamond marker (card.1.marker) centred under it on the dock's bottom edge; cards 2-5 have thin grey-bronze frames (card.5 has a teal frame). No card is disabled. Numerals: the concept's digits are more condensed than Crimson Pro, so width-fitted sizes render 2-4 px shorter in cap height (badge numbers: concept cap 16 px vs 12 px). In-world: unit HP bars are small dark-steel capsules (track ~50x8, fill inset 2-4 px): allies green, enemies red. Measured: world.ally.hp over the first archer (full) and world.enemy.hp over the first skeleton (~45%); other bars, approx. fill spans: allies x391-431 y374, x508-549 y378, x612-653 y388; enemy knight x970-989 y393 (~40%). The player wagon (world.wagon, left edge, with its own small green hp bar world.wagon.hp above the roof) and the enemy gate (world.gate, stone towers + red skull banner + spike palisade, cut by the right edge) bound the lane. Floating damage '27' (white, dark outline) sits above the struck skeleton. Scene lines (screen y): units' feet stand on a band y 463-492 (staggered depth: archer 2 ~465, knight 1 ~476, archer 1 ~480, knight 2 ~489, skeletons/enemy knight ~490-492; front-row feet line ~490); dirt road top edge y ~411, bottom edge y ~516 (grass verge below); foreground fence: post tops y ~514, top rail y ~528-545 (sloping), bottom rail y ~555-565; market stalls/back wall y ~285-390; horizon (base of the distant mountains / far fields, at the castle's base) y ~195; distant castle top (central spire tip, x ~837) y ~55; mountain ridges y ~80 (right) to ~145 (left). In game the two plates show courage (top, the concept's hull slot; flame icon rect sized like the concept's courage flame) and mana (second, blue crystal and royal-blue fill; courage's fill turns amber to match its flame so the two bars differ); the war wagon's health is drawn on the wagon instead. Magic cards wear a blue-centred cost badge."
}